WEBVTT

00:15.397 --> 00:17.983
You? A boyfriend? Give me a break.

00:18.900 --> 00:20.902
Is that guy okay in the head?

00:20.986 --> 00:23.864
You've played him. He doesn't know
you're really just a gorilla.

00:23.947 --> 00:24.948
Excuse me?

00:25.032 --> 00:28.243
What the heck? Jealous much?

00:28.326 --> 00:31.955
Keep that up, and he'll catch on.
You'll end up getting dumped again.

00:32.039 --> 00:36.168
Talk to me when you've figured out
your own love life.

00:36.251 --> 00:38.378
Though, I doubt you can.

00:38.462 --> 00:39.671
What...

00:40.589 --> 00:41.590
Shut up.

00:45.886 --> 00:47.137
Hey, don't let it get to you.

00:47.220 --> 00:49.097
Know what? You irritate me.

00:49.681 --> 00:52.601
SORRY, LET'S BREAK UP

00:57.189 --> 01:00.609
WHY?

01:00.692 --> 01:02.611
WHAT DID I DO?

01:07.574 --> 01:09.117
He hasn't read my messages.

01:09.201 --> 01:10.535
Wait, did he block me?

01:12.204 --> 01:13.872
It's over.

01:16.666 --> 01:19.169
<i>The end always comes
before it even begins.</i>

01:19.878 --> 01:23.507
<i>What did he like about me, to begin with?</i>

01:23.590 --> 01:25.383
<i>What did he know about me?</i>

01:28.470 --> 01:33.475
<i>Igarashi's only had eyes for Koyun...
Wish someone liked me like that too.</i>

01:35.227 --> 01:38.814
Koyun, what do you find
so repulsive about Igarashi?

01:40.690 --> 01:43.652
Well, I mean,
there's a lot to dislike about him.

01:43.735 --> 01:46.321
But he's so into you.

01:46.404 --> 01:47.405
AZUMI

01:48.031 --> 01:49.950
Isn't being liked good enough?

01:50.033 --> 01:51.284
Asking for more is greedy.

01:52.911 --> 01:53.912
You're right.

01:54.579 --> 01:57.457
I should be grateful he likes me at all.

01:58.667 --> 02:04.047
Igarashi might be the only person
who will keep liking me.

02:04.673 --> 02:05.674
Koyun?

02:07.801 --> 02:10.220
Where to next? Karaoke?

02:10.303 --> 02:12.430
Let's see.

02:12.514 --> 02:15.559
<i>Not long after, Koyun quit her club</i>

02:15.642 --> 02:18.061
<i>and started going out with Igarashi.</i>

02:19.354 --> 02:22.440
<i>Seriously, I shouldn't have said that.</i>

02:23.108 --> 02:25.235
Isn't being liked good enough?

02:25.318 --> 02:26.653
Asking for more is greedy.

02:27.320 --> 02:30.699
Is it... all my fault?

03:56.368 --> 04:01.957
THE RAMPARTS OF ICE

04:02.540 --> 04:06.962
EPISODE 6
NEW SEMESTER

04:09.923 --> 04:11.716
This year is almost over.

04:11.800 --> 04:12.801
AMAMIYA RESIDENCE
LIVING ROOM

04:12.884 --> 04:13.885
What's that all of a sudden?

04:13.969 --> 04:16.388
You're sad about
that one senior graduating, huh?

04:17.222 --> 04:19.057
Hey! That's not it!

04:19.140 --> 04:21.017
- You mean the one from the band?
- Yep.

04:21.101 --> 04:22.102
THIRD YEAR

04:22.185 --> 04:23.353
Wrong! You're dead wrong!

04:23.937 --> 04:24.980
Why don't you ask her out?

04:25.063 --> 04:26.439
Easy for you to say.

04:26.523 --> 04:30.318
You... You'll never understand how I feel!

04:30.819 --> 04:32.195
So you admit it, Hayato.

04:32.279 --> 04:33.863
What do you mean? I do too.

04:33.947 --> 04:35.490
No, you don't.

04:35.991 --> 04:38.660
You've never been in love before.

04:39.327 --> 04:40.745
That's rude.

04:40.829 --> 04:44.457
I've always loved my girlfriends
as much as they've loved me.

04:44.541 --> 04:46.710
- You're kinda like that!
- You're kinda like that!

04:46.793 --> 04:49.379
You're just neutral about everyone.

04:49.462 --> 04:51.006
But isn't that a good thing?

04:51.589 --> 04:53.049
Is it really so bad?

04:53.133 --> 04:54.134
It is.

04:54.217 --> 04:56.886
That's why you're always fine
after a break up.

04:56.970 --> 04:59.055
However I take it,

04:59.139 --> 05:03.393
the fact is,
they still wanted to break up, right?

05:03.476 --> 05:06.396
This is pointless, and I'm getting pissed.

05:06.980 --> 05:09.649
I hope one day,
you fall in love with someone

05:10.650 --> 05:12.610
who doesn't care about you at all.

05:12.694 --> 05:15.113
I hope she tramples all over your heart.

05:15.196 --> 05:16.197
That's right.

05:16.281 --> 05:17.907
We're friends, right?

05:18.491 --> 05:20.327
You hear that? Aren't they horrible?

05:23.872 --> 05:25.248
<i>She laughed.</i>

05:27.834 --> 05:29.002
How cute.

05:29.085 --> 05:31.004
STARE

05:35.550 --> 05:37.886
I'd never waste my time like that.

05:37.969 --> 05:39.262
- I figured.
- I figured.

05:41.431 --> 05:43.016
<i>Emotions.</i>

05:43.683 --> 05:47.020
<i>The more you let it show,
the more it gets used against you.</i>

05:51.107 --> 05:53.485
<i>These guys don't hold back.</i>

05:58.823 --> 06:01.284
<i>It's never made sense to me.</i>

06:01.868 --> 06:06.039
You tell me to set goals,
but you're against me chasing my dreams?

06:06.122 --> 06:08.958
Yours don't seem that serious.

06:09.042 --> 06:11.377
You just want to move out
and mess around all day.

06:11.461 --> 06:13.171
What's that? Say that again, bastard!

06:13.254 --> 06:14.756
- So noisy.
- Enough already!

06:14.839 --> 06:17.675
I wish he'd leave already,
that good-for-nothing punk.

06:18.802 --> 06:21.179
<i>You let your emotions take over
and end up in an argument...</i>

06:21.971 --> 06:25.433
<i>What "feeling" makes someone go that far?</i>

06:26.601 --> 06:29.479
<i>Emotions are nothing
but your brain sending signals, right?</i>

06:30.105 --> 06:32.398
<i>You should be able to control them.</i>

06:36.402 --> 06:37.570
Hey, hey!

06:41.157 --> 06:42.534
<i>Hikawa.</i>

06:49.124 --> 06:50.583
Sorry.

06:53.294 --> 06:55.713
<i>No, no, no, no!</i>

06:57.799 --> 06:59.467
<i>Stop it, brain.</i>

06:59.551 --> 07:02.220
<i>Stop it. Stop!</i>

07:02.303 --> 07:05.932
SOUND ASLEEP

07:06.015 --> 07:07.225
A sea slug?

07:07.308 --> 07:08.476
CLICK CLICK

07:08.560 --> 07:09.936
That's it, you look adorable.

07:10.019 --> 07:12.313
Over here? This angle? Yeah?

07:12.981 --> 07:14.566
ARE YOU FREE
THE DAY AFTER TOMORROW?

07:14.649 --> 07:15.650
It's Yota.

07:19.487 --> 07:21.573
SORRY, I GOT
CLUB ACTIVITIES ALL DAY

07:21.656 --> 07:22.907
GOTCHA

07:25.743 --> 07:26.744
Yota.

07:28.455 --> 07:30.165
Sorry, did I keep you waiting?

07:30.790 --> 07:31.791
Not in the slightest.

07:32.417 --> 07:34.252
You're really easy to spot.

07:35.003 --> 07:36.004
That's good.

07:37.005 --> 07:38.548
You're all puffy.

07:38.631 --> 07:40.341
And you're fluffy.

07:41.426 --> 07:43.136
Sorry to make you tag along.

07:43.219 --> 07:45.430
Don't be sorry. I wanted
to visit Miki at work too.

07:45.513 --> 07:46.806
EPISODE: OFF TO MIKI'S WORK!

07:46.890 --> 07:48.975
It's hard to stop by on your own.

07:49.851 --> 07:52.312
I marked the location on the map.

07:52.395 --> 07:54.063
Look at you, all prepared.

07:54.564 --> 07:56.149
Let's see.

07:56.232 --> 07:58.026
- Right this way.
- Thanks.

08:02.530 --> 08:03.656
Welcome...

08:03.740 --> 08:04.949
Hey, Koyun and Yota.

08:05.033 --> 08:07.619
OUT OF BREATH

08:07.702 --> 08:09.204
Did something happen?

08:09.287 --> 08:12.332
We were lost for 30 minutes.

08:12.415 --> 08:15.210
<i>What? How come?
It's a five-minute walk from the station.</i>

08:16.711 --> 08:18.630
I think you've got the wrong way.

08:18.713 --> 08:19.714
Say what?

08:20.590 --> 08:23.468
- Sorry I picked a weird time to come by.
- Thanks.

08:24.052 --> 08:26.304
I can't really talk
until the lunch rush is over.

08:26.804 --> 08:29.849
This is the most popular one,

08:29.933 --> 08:32.727
but I personally recommend
the one with avocado.

08:32.810 --> 08:34.979
Yota, you might like this one. It's spicy.

08:35.063 --> 08:37.190
- Then, I'll go with that one.
- That was quick.

08:37.690 --> 08:39.317
I need a minute.

08:39.400 --> 08:41.236
Take your time.

08:42.362 --> 08:45.031
- Then, I'll get the one with avocado.
- Okay.

08:45.532 --> 08:47.825
We have an order!
One chili and one avocado.

08:47.909 --> 08:49.160
Comin' right up.

08:49.244 --> 08:50.328
Miki.

08:51.704 --> 08:53.414
Are those two dating?

08:53.498 --> 08:57.252
What? As if. We're all just friends.

08:57.335 --> 08:58.378
Really?

08:58.461 --> 09:02.632
I mean, I think they look good together.

09:04.842 --> 09:08.012
The little one is next to the tall one.

09:08.096 --> 09:09.889
They're a perfect match, don't you think?

09:09.973 --> 09:11.891
How heartwarming.

09:11.975 --> 09:13.643
<i>Yota and Koyun?</i>

09:14.852 --> 09:17.605
<i>Now that he mentioned it,
I've never considered it before.</i>

09:18.106 --> 09:20.567
<i>If they ended up together,</i>

09:21.568 --> 09:23.111
<i>what would I do?</i>

09:25.280 --> 09:26.739
<i>I'd totally ship them.</i>

09:27.407 --> 09:29.200
<i>Yes. They're a match made in heaven.</i>

09:29.284 --> 09:31.995
<i>Koyun would be better off
with someone like Yota...</i>

09:33.371 --> 09:35.748
- No thanks.
- <i>No, no, no, no, no, no!</i>

09:36.583 --> 09:40.378
<i>I need to learn
to stay out of people's business.</i>

09:44.007 --> 09:45.758
<i>How do I bite into this?</i>

09:47.427 --> 09:49.387
How does it even fit in your mouth?

09:50.680 --> 09:51.598
AH

09:51.681 --> 09:52.599
PFFT

09:54.267 --> 09:56.102
What? What is it?

09:56.686 --> 09:59.689
<i>Yes... I can just see them working out.</i>

10:01.816 --> 10:03.109
I'm home.

10:04.110 --> 10:05.320
Welcome back.

10:05.403 --> 10:08.239
You're home. What about your job?

10:08.323 --> 10:09.741
I got off early today.

10:09.824 --> 10:13.536
Look. I took this pic of Ponta
lazing around like a sea slug.

10:13.620 --> 10:15.622
Aw, how precious.

10:16.247 --> 10:18.041
Send it to me too.

10:18.124 --> 10:19.250
Okay.

10:19.334 --> 10:21.878
Let's see, where's that chat with her...

10:22.462 --> 10:25.632
<i>What's this? Yota updated his profile pic.</i>

10:25.715 --> 10:26.883
<i>That's rare.</i>

10:27.884 --> 10:29.052
Why a burger?

10:31.220 --> 10:33.139
KOYUKI HIKAWA PROFILE UPDATED

10:33.222 --> 10:34.223
ACK

10:37.352 --> 10:39.145
What?

10:39.729 --> 10:41.939
Minato, have you sent the photo yet?

10:42.023 --> 10:43.399
What are you doing?

10:43.983 --> 10:47.070
<i>What does it all mean?</i>

10:53.868 --> 10:54.952
<i>I knew it.</i>

10:55.662 --> 10:57.413
<i>Hikawa's got a crush on...</i>

11:00.041 --> 11:01.876
GRADE 1 CLASS 6

11:01.959 --> 11:04.212
The winter break came and went in a flash.

11:04.295 --> 11:07.507
Yota, your profile pic...
What's up with that?

11:09.550 --> 11:10.551
Oh, that?

11:11.719 --> 11:12.720
NONCHALANT

11:12.804 --> 11:13.971
I'm matching with Koyun.

11:14.055 --> 11:15.056
Miki drew it.

11:15.556 --> 11:16.766
What? Miki?

11:17.809 --> 11:22.063
You see, the illustrations on the menu
were drawn by yours truly.

11:22.146 --> 11:24.524
- Wow, that's amazing!
- This one that's alive is cute.

11:24.607 --> 11:25.608
THE ONE THAT'S ALIVE

11:25.691 --> 11:27.777
Keep the compliments coming!

11:27.860 --> 11:30.655
We looked at it when Koyun and I
visited Miki at her work.

11:30.738 --> 11:31.739
CRACK

11:32.323 --> 11:33.658
Just the two of you?

11:33.741 --> 11:37.495
Yeah. I asked if you were free,
but you said you had practice all day.

11:38.830 --> 11:40.248
<i>Now that you mention it...</i>

11:41.457 --> 11:46.087
When making plans, it's considerate to let
people know what you're inviting them to.

11:47.338 --> 11:48.339
Yota.

11:50.258 --> 11:52.385
It hurts to be left out.

11:52.468 --> 11:55.096
You're unusually honest,
and it's creeping me out.

11:55.179 --> 11:56.639
That's harsh.

11:56.722 --> 11:57.723
GRADE 1 CLASS 2

11:57.807 --> 12:01.686
Lastly, we still haven't decided
the library committee member.

12:03.729 --> 12:06.858
<i>Work made the winter break fly by.</i>

12:07.900 --> 12:09.944
<i>It was so boring.</i>

12:10.027 --> 12:11.737
<i>The shifts are flexible,</i>

12:11.821 --> 12:13.406
<i>the customers are chill,</i>

12:13.489 --> 12:16.492
<i>and hardly anyone my age comes in,
so it's the ideal job in a way.</i>

12:16.576 --> 12:18.119
<i>I hope they don't go out of business.</i>

12:19.036 --> 12:22.748
Who here isn't
a part of a club or a committee?

12:32.467 --> 12:34.010
LIBRARY COMMITTEE MEMBERS (2)
HIKAWA - SHIMOJIMA

12:34.093 --> 12:36.012
HIKAWA - BAM

12:36.095 --> 12:38.514
LIBRARY REP RESPONSIBILITIES

12:38.598 --> 12:41.309
Sounded like we'll have our hands full.

12:41.392 --> 12:45.021
We have to stick around till school's out
when we're manning the desk.

12:45.104 --> 12:46.481
DEAD SILENT

12:47.273 --> 12:49.025
<i>What an awkward silence.</i>

12:51.235 --> 12:53.362
<i>I'll have to adjust my work schedule.</i>

12:55.781 --> 12:58.910
A thought just occurred to me.
You're not in any clubs either, right?

12:58.993 --> 12:59.994
FLUSTERED

13:00.077 --> 13:01.662
No, I'm in art club.

13:01.746 --> 13:06.501
We draw freely, so people tend
to think we have it easy. There's that.

13:06.584 --> 13:08.544
FLUSTERED THAT KOYUN
SUDDENLY MADE CONVERSATION

13:10.129 --> 13:13.883
The sports clubs must think
we've got all the time in the world.

13:13.966 --> 13:15.718
That's what they think of us.

13:15.801 --> 13:16.802
PISSED OFF

13:16.886 --> 13:17.929
STARE

13:18.012 --> 13:19.805
<i>Oh, no!
Did I sound like I was complaining?</i>

13:21.098 --> 13:22.391
That's irritating.

13:23.518 --> 13:26.646
I hate people who make assumptions
and look down on others.

13:28.231 --> 13:31.359
I thought this school
didn't really have that problem.

13:31.984 --> 13:34.153
<i>Wait, what? Did she just...</i>

13:35.238 --> 13:36.239
<i>try to relate to me?</i>

13:38.658 --> 13:39.659
That's...

13:41.327 --> 13:42.328
Sorry.

13:42.912 --> 13:44.413
I'm going that way for a bit.

13:45.081 --> 13:46.082
Sure.

13:46.666 --> 13:47.667
Catch you later.

13:48.960 --> 13:50.461
Yeah, see you.

13:51.504 --> 13:55.091
<i>Hikawa wasn't as scary as I thought.</i>

13:58.010 --> 13:59.011
Yota.

13:59.971 --> 14:00.972
Koyun.

14:04.559 --> 14:06.269
- Happy New Year.
- Happy New Year.

14:11.190 --> 14:12.733
What about your club activities, Yota?

14:13.317 --> 14:14.360
No club today.

14:14.443 --> 14:15.903
The gym is in use.

14:16.404 --> 14:17.405
I see.

14:18.155 --> 14:20.992
- Have you been out here all this time?
- Yeah.

14:21.659 --> 14:25.705
I like to gaze up at the sky
absent-mindedly like this.

14:26.414 --> 14:27.498
Really?

14:27.999 --> 14:30.209
Is there something on your mind?

14:30.710 --> 14:32.128
No, not really.

14:33.337 --> 14:35.089
I don't think about anything.

14:38.467 --> 14:39.468
I see.

14:42.638 --> 14:43.639
<i>This is peaceful.</i>

14:44.599 --> 14:47.768
<i>Both the time drifting by slowly
and Yota too.</i>

14:49.103 --> 14:52.732
<i>Time flows slowly,
as if he's a drifting cloud.</i>

14:54.650 --> 14:57.111
<i>"Yota" means "the sun,"
but he's more like a cloud.</i>

14:57.194 --> 14:58.195
CHUCKLE

14:59.238 --> 15:01.574
<i>Not thinking about anything is hard.</i>

15:03.826 --> 15:07.246
<i>Thoughts are constantly
running through my head.</i>

15:07.747 --> 15:10.708
<i>The smallest things make me overthink,
and I get worked up over them.</i>

15:11.208 --> 15:13.377
<i>I get tired of myself for that.</i>

15:15.671 --> 15:17.381
<i>Yota and I are polar opposites.</i>

15:19.634 --> 15:22.845
<i>I can't imagine Yota
getting hung up over the little things</i>

15:22.929 --> 15:25.890
<i>or worrying about them like I do.</i>

15:28.851 --> 15:29.936
<i>It must be nice.</i>

15:31.354 --> 15:33.064
<i>I want to be like him.</i>

15:39.570 --> 15:42.406
Hey, Amamiya, stop getting distracted!

15:42.907 --> 15:45.242
<i>Is this... actually happening?</i>

15:54.460 --> 15:56.462
<i>I read from start to finish.</i>

15:57.338 --> 15:59.548
<i>There are less visitors
than I anticipated.</i>

16:01.300 --> 16:02.301
Is that an art book?

16:02.385 --> 16:05.346
Yeah. Looking at it helps me learn.

16:06.097 --> 16:08.599
You're a great artist, Shimojima.

16:08.683 --> 16:10.267
I'm really not...

16:10.351 --> 16:12.895
Hold on, you've seen my drawings before?

16:12.979 --> 16:14.271
Oh, yeah.

16:14.355 --> 16:18.234
When we were doing oil paintings,
I could see your canvas from my spot.

16:19.610 --> 16:21.529
Sorry to peek without asking.

16:21.612 --> 16:22.947
SCURRYING AWAY
EMOTIONAL DISTANCE

16:23.030 --> 16:25.282
What? Don't worry about it. Come back.

16:28.369 --> 16:30.538
- See you later.
- See you tomorrow.

16:33.457 --> 16:36.335
<i>Maybe I should look at some art books too.</i>

16:36.419 --> 16:38.295
<i>I wonder what art book
I should start with.</i>

16:38.379 --> 16:40.297
GROWL

16:47.263 --> 16:48.848
<i>His head is sticking out.</i>

16:50.725 --> 16:52.059
CLEARLY YOTA

16:53.686 --> 16:54.687
THUD

16:54.770 --> 16:56.355
I'm sorry.

16:56.439 --> 16:57.857
It's you, Koyun.

16:57.940 --> 16:59.483
You scared me.

17:01.402 --> 17:05.114
Geez, it's dangerous
if you get in my blind spot.

17:05.197 --> 17:07.324
You make it sound like you're a truck.

17:07.992 --> 17:09.702
What are you buying, Koyun?

17:09.785 --> 17:13.622
- I'm a little hungry. Anything will do.
- Same here.

17:13.706 --> 17:15.207
FREE GIFT WITH A HOT SNACK
CHECK YOUR RECEIPT

17:15.291 --> 17:17.460
Are you in a hurry to get home, Koyun?

17:22.798 --> 17:24.550
This is warming my hands up.

17:26.052 --> 17:27.928
It's gonna get cold.

17:28.012 --> 17:31.015
What about dinner at your house, Yota?
Is that okay?

17:31.098 --> 17:32.475
Of course, it's okay.

17:34.894 --> 17:37.146
- I can eat it all easily.
- That figures.

17:37.229 --> 17:38.230
SECOND ONE

17:39.023 --> 17:42.443
You've been staying late
at school recently.

17:42.526 --> 17:45.279
I'm on library duty right now.

17:45.362 --> 17:47.782
Did they force it on you?

17:48.491 --> 17:50.493
No, that's not what it is.

17:51.786 --> 17:53.871
Come to think of it, is that what it is?

17:56.082 --> 18:00.169
But I've become interested in things
I never thought I'd look at before.

18:00.252 --> 18:02.588
So it's not that bad. So far.

18:03.172 --> 18:05.091
I have a lot of time to space out.

18:05.174 --> 18:06.634
Really?

18:06.717 --> 18:08.761
I should've done it too.

18:09.345 --> 18:12.181
You don't have time for that
with your club activities.

18:14.600 --> 18:17.812
But I want to spend some time zoning out.

18:20.523 --> 18:24.401
<i>Talking with Yota makes me feel at ease.</i>

18:26.987 --> 18:27.988
<i>It feels warm.</i>

18:36.080 --> 18:38.415
The fries aren't salty enough today.

18:38.499 --> 18:40.793
<i>Hikawa and Yota...</i>

18:45.089 --> 18:46.590
<i>I wish they wouldn't...</i>

18:49.760 --> 18:53.848
<i>Even if you fall in love with Yota,
you'll just end up suffering.</i>

18:59.728 --> 19:01.564
Yota, is your house that way?

19:01.647 --> 19:04.567
Yeah. But I'll walk you to the station.

19:04.650 --> 19:05.818
You don't have to.

19:05.901 --> 19:09.113
But I'm worried you'll get lost.

19:09.196 --> 19:10.364
I won't get lost.

19:13.409 --> 19:14.535
Yota!

19:18.998 --> 19:21.041
That scared me.

19:21.125 --> 19:23.502
Turn on your lights. Geez.

19:26.505 --> 19:27.506
SHE SLID

19:27.590 --> 19:29.008
Are you okay?

19:29.091 --> 19:30.885
Yeah. Sorry.

19:31.552 --> 19:33.137
Here, hold on to me.

19:33.721 --> 19:34.805
There you go.

19:47.484 --> 19:48.485
Is something wrong?

19:49.778 --> 19:50.863
No.

19:51.864 --> 19:52.865
Just now...

19:54.366 --> 19:56.452
When I was small...

19:57.536 --> 20:00.206
I just suddenly remembered my dad.

20:01.415 --> 20:02.708
It felt floaty.

20:02.791 --> 20:03.834
FLOATY

20:03.918 --> 20:06.212
<i>Wait, what am I even explaining?</i>

20:08.464 --> 20:10.883
It's okay.
You can call me the wrong name sometimes.

20:10.966 --> 20:13.844
That's what elementary school kids do
to their teachers.

20:17.765 --> 20:18.849
<i>I see.</i>

20:19.683 --> 20:20.684
<i>That's why.</i>

20:22.811 --> 20:25.356
<i>I wonder how my dad is doing.</i>

20:30.319 --> 20:31.779
If you were my daughter,

20:31.862 --> 20:34.573
I'd have to go to the Lost Child Center
every time we went out.

20:34.657 --> 20:37.368
I told you I wouldn't get lost every time.

20:39.828 --> 20:40.829
Yota?

20:49.838 --> 20:51.048
What are you doing here?

20:51.840 --> 20:53.592
I forgot to buy a lot of things.

20:54.677 --> 20:56.512
What about Haruto and Sakura?

20:57.638 --> 20:59.014
Dad's at home.

20:59.098 --> 21:01.433
He's already back home today.

21:01.517 --> 21:03.852
- Did you need dinner today at all?
- <i>A family member?</i>

21:03.936 --> 21:06.522
- Yes, I do. Sorry I didn't contact you.
- <i>Is she his sister?</i>

21:06.605 --> 21:09.817
<i>Maybe I should go home.</i>

21:09.900 --> 21:11.068
Yota.

21:11.151 --> 21:14.655
Well, I'll be back soon after I walk
my friend to the station.

21:16.949 --> 21:18.117
Okay.

21:18.617 --> 21:19.868
Be careful out there.

21:32.506 --> 21:34.508
Yota, was that okay?

21:35.801 --> 21:37.970
Well...

21:38.887 --> 21:40.180
- Your sister--
- My mom.

21:43.475 --> 21:46.312
She's my mother.

21:46.395 --> 21:50.190
?? YEARS OLD - 16 YEARS OLD = ??

21:50.274 --> 21:51.567
What?

21:52.151 --> 21:53.944
We're not related by blood though.

21:55.237 --> 21:58.866
My real mother died
when I was in elementary school.

22:06.206 --> 22:08.876
Oh, sorry.
I guess that's a natural reaction.

22:08.959 --> 22:10.210
Oh, no...

22:11.337 --> 22:13.964
It's been a while, so I'm fine.

22:14.798 --> 22:15.924
Right now,

22:17.009 --> 22:18.719
the family I have
is what feels normal to me.

23:50.269 --> 23:55.274
Subtitle translation by Megumi Hunter
